    {
      "code": "MODEL_ANCHOR_LATE",
      "note": "Already named in the v1 anchor README error table as a verification code (not in any schema enum). Same name, same meaning; v2 adds it to the append Error enum. Neither is renamed."
    },
    {
      "code": "KIND_IMMUTABLE",
      "note": "v1 README (WP-11 decision 8) says KIND_IMMUTABLE is not used because a relabel is a second freeze for the key (FREEZE_KEY_EXISTS). v2 writers now receive KIND_IMMUTABLE for that case, which takes precedence over FREEZE_KEY_EXISTS; v1 writers still receive FREEZE_KEY_EXISTS. A behaviour difference, not a name conflict."
    },
    {
      "code": "FREEZE_INCOMPLETE",
      "note": "v1 defines it for a freeze naming absent RealityTrace records (NT-33 b). G NT-33 uses it also for (a) RealityTrace records without a case record and (c) a missing anchor; these arise at execution gating (execution-episode-ref.v1), not at append. Extension of the same code, not a rename."
    },
    {
      "code": "FREEZE_MISSING",
      "note": "v1 defines it for episode.settled with no freeze and mentions the delegation refusal; v2 defines the execution-gate meaning (NT-32) as: no RealityTrace records and no case record. No name conflict."
    }
  ],
